{"nangchen":{"img":"/images/states/nangchen.jpg","cr":{"a":"Wikiwakhan","l":"CC BY 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Gar_monastery_(Ga%27er_in_Chinese),_Nangq%C3%AAn_county.jpg"}},"nagar":{"img":"/images/states/nagar.jpg","cr":{"a":"Zoeperkoe","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tell_Brak_001.jpg"}},"naiman-khanate":{"img":"/images/states/naiman-khanate.jpg","cr":{"a":"Khiruge","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naiman_Khanate.png"}},"nilgiri-state":{"img":"/images/states/nilgiri-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Great Britain India Office","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keonjhar-Rairakhol_Imperial_Gazetteer.jpg"}},"nurmekund":{"img":"/images/states/nurmekund.jpg","cr":{"a":"No machine-readable author provided. 藏骨集团 assumed (based on copyright claims).","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Estonian_counties.png"}},"new-spain":{"img":"/images/states/new-spain.jpg","cr":{"a":"Eddo","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Viceroyalty_of_New_Spain.svg"}},"nagpur-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/nagpur-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"Joseph E. Schwartzberg","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhonsle_kingdom_of_Nagpur.png"}},"narsinghpur-state":{"img":"/images/states/narsinghpur-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Great Britain India Office","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daspalla-Nayagarh-Imperial_Gazetteer.jpg"}},"nizari-ismaili-state":{"img":"/images/states/nizari-ismaili-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Jolle","l":"CC BY 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alamut.png"}},"netherlands-new-guinea":{"img":"/images/states/netherlands-new-guinea.jpg","cr":{"a":"Zscout370","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg"}},"new-zealand":{"img":"/images/states/new-zealand.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Albert Hastings Markham Vector: Zscout370, Hugh Jass, s. File history","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Zealand.svg"}},"neo-inca-state":{"img":"/images/states/neo-inca-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Made and uploaded by Huhsunqu.","l":"CC BY-SA 2.5","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Inca_Empire.svg"}},"northern-yan":{"img":"/images/states/northern-yan.jpg","cr":{"a":"SY","l":"CC BY 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sixteen_Kingdoms_423_AD_(2).jpg"}},"naxos-sicily":{"t":"The first Greek colony in Sicily, founded by Chalcidians in 734 BCE beneath Mount Etna and destroyed by Dionysius I in 403 BCE.","o":"According to Thucydides, Chalcidians from Euboea, joined by Naxians from the Aegean, founded Naxos in 734 BCE on the Schisò headland below modern Taormina, led by Theocles. As the first landfall for ships crossing from Greece, it became the starting point for Greek colonisation of the island.","r":"Naxos was small but symbolically important: its altar of Apollo Archegetes, \u0027the Founder\u0027, was where envoys sailing from Sicily to Greece made sacrifice. Within a few years it sent out settlers to found Leontini and Catana. It grew vines on the slopes of Etna, and its coins with Dionysus and a satyr are celebrated. Hippocrates of Gela subdued it around 495 BCE, and later it was often allied with Athens and Leontini against Syracuse.","e":"Dionysius I captured Naxos by treachery in 403 BCE, sold its people into slavery and gave its land to the Sicels. In 358 BCE survivors and Sicels founded Tauromenium on the hill above. Excavations at Giardini Naxos have revealed the walls, sanctuaries and street grid.","re":"Greek religion","la":"Ionic Greek","img":"/images/states/naxos-sicily.jpg","cr":{"a":"Alun Salt from Derby and Leicester, UK","l":"CC BY-SA 2.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walls_at_Naxos,_Sicily_(71735239).jpg"}},"neutral-confederacy":{"img":"/images/states/neutral-confederacy.jpg","cr":{"a":"The Hsinging Tree","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Neutral_Confederacy_in_1600.png"}},"northern-liang":{"img":"/images/states/northern-liang.jpg","cr":{"a":"SY","l":"CC BY 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sixteen_Kingdoms_436_AD_(2).jpg"}},"new-hebrides-condominium":{"img":"/images/states/new-hebrides-condominium.jpg","cr":{"a":"TUBS","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vanuatu_on_the_globe_(Polynesia_centered).svg"}},"nagas-of-padmavati":{"img":"/images/states/nagas-of-padmavati.jpg","cr":{"a":"Thomas Lessman (Contact!)","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East-Hem_300ad.jpg"}},"neustria":{"img":"/images/states/neustria.jpg","cr":{"a":"Kairom13","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francia_714.png"}},"north-eastern-rhodesia":{"img":"/images/states/north-eastern-rhodesia.jpg","cr":{"a":"Mangwanani","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_South_Africa_Company.svg"}},"naranjo":{"img":"/images/states/naranjo.jpg","cr":{"a":"Rudy Canales","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sitio_el_naranjo_1.jpg"}},"narsinghgarh-state":{"img":"/images/states/narsinghgarh-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"QuadrangleDinglePingle","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narsinghgarh_Flag.png"}},"novgorod-republic":{"img":"/images/states/novgorod-republic.jpg","cr":{"a":"Gabagool","l":"CC BY 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Novgorod1400.png"}},"nationalist-government":{"img":"/images/states/nationalist-government.jpg","cr":{"a":"Sekisama","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Emblem_of_the_Republic_of_China.svg"}},"novantae":{"t":"People of Galloway in south-west Scotland, named by Ptolemy, whose peninsula and towns faced the Irish Sea.","o":"Ptolemy lists the Novantae in south-western Scotland, giving their name to a peninsula, the Novantarum Promontorium, usually identified with the Rhins of Galloway, and naming two towns, Locopibia and Rerigonium. They grew from Iron Age communities living in duns, crannogs and small forts along the coast and inland valleys of Galloway.","r":"No rulers or written records survive. Agricola\u0027s campaigns of about 81 probably brought Roman troops into Galloway, and forts were built at Glenlochar and Gatehouse of Fleet. Their position on the Irish Sea gave them close contact with Ireland and the Isle of Man, and their society was rural and pastoral.","e":"Roman control of the region was brief, and the Novantae disappear from the written record after Ptolemy. Their territory later formed part of British kingdoms of the north, possibly Rheged, before Northumbrian expansion into Galloway in the 7th and 8th centuries.","re":"Celtic polytheism","la":"Common Brittonic","c":"low"},"north-borneo":{"img":"/images/states/north-borneo.jpg","cr":{"a":"Orange Tuesday (talk)","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Borneo_(1902%E2%80%931946).svg"}},"nadruvians":{"img":"/images/states/nadruvians.jpg","cr":{"a":"Renata3","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prussian_clans_13th_century.png"}},"north-western-rhodesia":{"img":"/images/states/north-western-rhodesia.jpg","cr":{"a":"Mangwanani","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_South_Africa_Company.svg"}},"north-german-confederation":{"img":"/images/states/north-german-confederation.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Adolf Soetbeer, Otto von Bismarck Vector: B1mbo, Madden","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany_(1867%E2%80%931918).svg"}},"neutral-moresnet":{"img":"/images/states/neutral-moresnet.jpg","cr":{"a":"ThrashedParanoid","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Moresnet.svg"}},"nayagarh-state":{"img":"/images/states/nayagarh-state.jp